m2_alpha_llm: the s1_alpha_llm mission as a small fleet.

One shoreside community (MOOSDB 9000, pShare 9200) runs pMarineViewer with
the chat pane and pLLMAgent. Each simulated vehicle (abe, ben, ... on
9001+/9201+) is its own community with the blank alpha helm and its own
pBehaviorTree. The model names a vehicle (or all) in every tool;
uFldShoreBroker carries DEPLOY_ABE, BT_TREE_ABE and friends down to abe as
the bare variables, and each vehicle's uFldNodeBroker sends its node
report, its plan's map shapes and its status back up renamed with its
name (BT_STATE_ABE, BT_CHAT_ABE, MISSION_ABE); pLLMAgent and the chat pane
route by that suffix.

  ./launch.sh [--amt=N] [--nogui] [--just_make] [time_warp]

launch.sh runs launch_vehicle.sh once per vehicle and launch_shoreside.sh,
filling meta_vehicle.moos, meta_vehicle.bhv and meta_shoreside.moos with
nsplug (the targ_* files are the results), then runs uMAC on the
shoreside; quitting uMAC or Ctrl-C halts everything. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
must be set in the shell for the chat to answer; without it the fleet
still runs from the viewer's buttons (they act on every vehicle; there is
no mouse context) and from uPokeDB.

The shoreside also runs uFldTeam (moos-ivp-team): teams of vehicles as
objects. TEAM_CMD forms a team (its members take the team color on the
map), moves its center of mass with every member keeping its offset, or
puts it in a formation (line, column, wedge, circle ...) that holds at rest
and moves as a body behind a virtual leader the members trail with
BHV_Trail (the formation block in meta_vehicle.bhv). TEAM_REPORT_<NAME>,
TEAM_<NAME>_X/_Y/... and TEAM_MISSION_<NAME> come back. pLLMAgent gets the
team_* tools from the team capability set (a capability_dir = team line),
and follow from the contact set (capability_dir = contact): one vehicle
trails another along its exact track at a set distance, through the
BHV_Convoy block in meta_vehicle.bhv (TASK = convoy, CONVOY_UPDATE).

Beside it runs one pBehaviorTree with a plan slot per team (teams_var =
TEAM_LIST): a team's variables carry its suffix (BT_TREE_RED, BT_STATE_RED,
BT_CHAT_RED, BT_PLAN_RED ...), so a plan reaches red the way a vehicle's
reaches abe, two teams run two plans at once, and a disbanded team's plan
is halted with it. A team plan starts with a bare <Team> (the whole team,
from TEAM_REPORT_<NAME>) and drives no vehicle itself: each Member block,
or a leaf with a vname, goes down to that vehicle as its own plan and the
block waits on BT_STATE_<VNAME>; Report lines come back up as
BT_REPORT_<VNAME> and Signal goes down as BT_SIGNAL; the team leaves
(TeamFormation, TeamGoto ...) run on the executor and post TEAM_CMD. The
team's report shows the plan (plan=, plan_state=). pLLMAgent learns the
teams from TEAM_LIST too (run_plan vname=red) and the fleet prompt tells
the model to form a team, then plan for it. Vehicles a plan does not list
are left alone; a member taken out of its team is taken over, and the team
plan ends. plans/team_wedge_south.xml is a plan of team leaves (form a
wedge, move south), plans/team_line_south.xml the full Member form (each
member reports at the line, the coordinator signals the move south),
plans/team_box.xml the compact form, plans/follow_ben.xml a vehicle
reacting to another through the contact variables (BEN_RANGE). A member
may itself be a team (a team of teams; see the moos-ivp-bt README), which
this mission keeps out to stay minimal.

Without the model, from this directory:
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos BT_TREE_FILE_ABE=plans/box_goto.xml
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos TASK_BEN=waypoint WPT_UPDATE_BEN=points=40,-40 DEPLOY_BEN=true MOOS_MANUAL_OVERRIDE_BEN=false
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos BT_REPLY_ABE=yes
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos TEAM_CMD:=action=create,name=red,members=abe:ben
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos BT_TREE_FILE_RED=plans/team_wedge_south.xml
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos BT_CMD_RED=halt
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos BT_CMD_ALL=halt
  uXMS targ_shoreside.moos BT_STATE_RED BT_PLAN_RED BT_MEMBERS_RED BT_STATE_ABE BT_STATE_BEN BT_REPORT_ABE BT_REPORT_BEN
  pBehaviorTree --check=plans/team_line_south.xml --team --roster=abe,ben
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos TEAM_CMD:=action=formation,name=red,shape=line,spacing=30
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos TEAM_CMD:=action=goto,name=red,x=60,y=-160
  uXMS targ_shoreside.moos TEAM_LIST TEAM_REPORT_RED TEAM_MISSION_RED TEAM_EVENT

This is the shape the MCTF mission takes later: pLLMAgent joins its
shoreside block, pBehaviorTree and the bridge lines join meta_surveyor.moos.
